    "body": "## Problem\n\nChanging `'undolevels'` only synchronizes the undo state of the current buffer.\n\nIf a non-current buffer is modified while `'undolevels'` is `-1`, then `'undolevels'` is restored to a non-negative value, that buffer remains unsynchronized. Modifying it again can leave the undo state inconsistent and cause a crash in `u_savecommon()`.\n\nThe same issue affects buffer-local `'undolevels'` changes because the synchronization is performed on the current buffer instead of the target buffer.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd `u_sync_buf()` to synchronize the undo state of a specific buffer while preserving `u_sync()` for current-buffer callers.\n\nWhen the global `'undolevels'` value changes, synchronize every buffer that inherits the global value. When a buffer-local value changes, synchronize the target buffer directly.\n\nAdd regression tests covering both global and buffer-local `'undolevels'` changes on non-current buffers, verifying that the subsequent edit does not crash and creates a valid undo entry.\n\nFixes #42447",
